abstract:
Fraud is 0.1% of transactions, cancer is 1% of scans, churn is 5% of users. A model that predicts "no" every time is 99.9% accurate and completely worthless. This topic covers the metrics that survive imbalance, the resampling family from random oversampling to SMOTE and its variants, class weights, threshold tuning — and the measured result that threshold tuning usually beats all the fancy sampling.}
